    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and re-shaped household duplicate handling in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (plus doc updates in `openapi.yml`).\n\n**`householdId` is now always computed** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.householdId`): the first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`. Last name is normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase); owners with no postcode get `null` (no household basis, consistent with the existing possible-duplicate rule). Previously it hashed `lastName + address` (16 chars) and was only set when `sharesHousehold` was true.\n\n**In `addOwner`:**\n- `owner.setHouseholdId(householdId(owner))` now runs unconditionally, so the id is derived from `(lastName, postcode)` for every owner rather than being created by `sharesHousehold`.\n- Added `rejectHouseholdDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)`: if another owner already has the same computed `householdId`, the create is rejected with 409 (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`) **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set, in which case it's created as a declared member.\n- `possibleDuplicateOf` is skipped for declared members (`sharesHousehold ? null : possibleDuplicateOf(owner)`), so a declared household member is never flagged as a suspected duplicate.\n\nThe exact-identity duplicate check (`telephone|email|householdId`) still runs first, and the household check reuses the same `existingOwnerMatches`/`findAllOwners` machinery so it has identical deleted-owner semantics.\n\nThe one behavior nuance worth flagging: `sharesHousehold` bypasses only the broader household (same last-name + postcode) block; a truly identical owner (same telephone + email + household) is still rejected by the exact-identity check even with `sharesHousehold` set. The spec's \"only bypasses the duplicate block\" language is ambiguous there, and this keeps a genuine same-person duplicate from slipping through \u2014 no test exercises that case either way.",
